  "mechanisms": [
    "Immutable typed draft fixes source revision/acceptance event/policy, storage UUID, actor authority/mount, explicit destination and key reference/fingerprint. Draft creation makes no remote contact.",
    "Approval/cancellation bind exact definition hash, intent ID and state revision. Intent/events/actor-private idempotency receipts commit together.",
    "Every new domain relation has forced tenant/partner and restrictive actor row policies. Runtime transactions check all 15 relations live.",
    "Database-wide retained session locks bound this initial profile to two streams. Real independent pools exercise capacity. A worker executes one specified intent, with no unbounded queue scan.",
    "Database-clock leases renew every five seconds, expire after 30 seconds, and issue a strictly growing attempt fence; expired staging can claim a distinct generated temporary file.",
    "Sequential 32 KiB streaming checks current source authority, lease and storage identity. The client bounds receiver-controlled frames before library allocation.",
    "Remote fsync, close and exact read-back precede committing publishing. Atomic no-overwrite OpenSSH hardlink publication precedes final read-back and persisted observed receipt.",
    "Lost publication acknowledgment/worker/local receipt commit produces ambiguity; no automatic retransmission is allowed. Missing or consumed remote files remain ambiguous.",
    "Read-only exact final-file observation can record recovered integrity evidence, without claiming file-sync acknowledgment or business processing. Failed reconciliation observation is journaled.",
    "Stock native journey verifies competing processes, actual pre-publication worker kill, real expiry/new fence, source corruption, host mismatch, path/symlink/storage/collision/actor/grant/revocation denial."
  ],
